{"id":"nursing-homes-after-change-of-owner","title":"Nursing homes that changed hands: nursing hours, rent, related-company balances and citations before and after","question":"When a Bay Area nursing home is sold, what happens to staffing, to rent and to the money owed by related companies?","finding":"48 Bay Area nursing homes changed owner between 2019 and 2024 and filed a full-year State report on each side of the sale. Their nursing hours per resident day moved by a middle figure of 6.2% from the last year before the sale to the latest year after, against 2.8% for Bay Area homes that did not change hands over the same years; 23 of the 48 did worse than those peers. Rent and lease cost per resident day moved 58.0% at the sold homes against 3.7% at peers; in dollars, the 48 homes reported $35.6 million of rent and lease cost in their last year before the sale and $67.3 million in their latest year. 15 homes show both nursing hours below peers and rent above peers. At 25 the amount owed by related companies rose by $1 million or more. State citations of class AA, A or B in the two years before and after the sale, where both windows are on file (48 homes): 27 before, 34 after. Furthest below peers on nursing hours: Mountain View Healthcare Center (Mountain View; to Cirby Holdings LLC on 2022-10-01; 4.73 to 3.65 hours); City View Post Acute (San Francisco; to Pine Street SNF LLC on 2023-05-01; 4.9 to 3.93 hours); Atherton Park Post-Acute (Menlo Park; to Carpinteria LLC on 2019-08-01; 4.09 to 3.64 hours).","how":"Changes of ownership are from the federal change-of-ownership file (effective 2019 or later; buyer and seller as named there), joined to the State financial reports through the State listing, which carries the federal certification number, the State facility number and the State financial-report number for each home: all exact identifiers. Nursing hours are registered-nurse, vocational-nurse and nurse-assistant productive hours plus the same staff from registries, divided by resident days; rent is the lease and rental line per resident day; the related balance is amounts due from related parties less amounts due to them. \"Before\" is the last full-year report before the year of the sale and \"after\" the latest full-year report after it. Peers are Bay Area homes with no change of owner on file, over the same two years. Related payments as a share of expenses are from the complete data sets for 2019 and 2025. Citations are class AA, A and B from the archived State file (to 2020) and the State dashboard (2021 to 13 November 2026).","limits":"A buyer often takes over a home in trouble, so falling hours can continue a slide that began under the seller, and a new owner may change how hours and rent are reported. Rent usually rises at a sale because the building is revalued or leased from a landlord; that is ordinary where the landlord is unrelated. Resident mix changed sharply over 2020 to 2022. Reports for 2023 to 2025 are as submitted, not audited. A related-party balance is a claim the home still holds. Small homes swing on a few staff.","tier":"REDFLAG","columns":[{"k":"home","t":"Nursing home","type":"org"},{"k":"city","t":"City","type":"text"},{"k":"changed","t":"Changed owner","type":"date"},{"k":"buyer","t":"Buyer (federal file)","type":"org"},{"k":"seller","t":"Seller (federal file)","type":"org"},{"k":"before","t":"Report year before","type":"year"},{"k":"after","t":"Report year after","type":"year"},{"k":"hoursBefore","t":"Nursing hours per resident day, before","type":"times"},{"k":"hoursAfter","t":"After","type":"times"},{"k":"hoursChange","t":"Change","type":"pct"},{"k":"peersHoursChange","t":"Peers, same years","type":"pct"},{"k":"leaseBefore","t":"Rent per resident day, before","type":"usd"},{"k":"leaseAfter","t":"After","type":"usd"},{"k":"relBefore","t":"Owed by related companies (net), before","type":"usd"},{"k":"relAfter","t":"After","type":"usd"},{"k":"relPaid2019","t":"Paid to related companies, share of expenses, 2019","type":"pct"},{"k":"relPaid2025","t":"2025","type":"pct"},{"k":"citesBefore","t":"State citations, 2 years before","type":"int"},{"k":"citesAfter","t":"2 years after","type":"int"}],"rows":[{"home":"Mountain View Healthcare Center","city":"Mountain View","changed":"2022-10-01","buyer":"Cirby Holdings LLC","seller":"Palmero Enterprises Inc","before":2021,"after":2025,"hoursBefore":4.73,"hoursAfter":3.65,"hoursChange":-0.229,"leaseBefore":0.91,"leaseAfter":35.79,"relBefore":0,"relAfter":-3324920,"relPaid2019":0.0,"relPaid2025":0.061,"citesBefore":1,"citesAfter":5,"peersHoursChange":0.027},{"home":"City View Post Acute","city":"San Francisco","changed":"2023-05-01","buyer":"Pine Street SNF LLC","seller":"Ghc Of San Fran 180 LLC","before":2022,"after":2025,"hoursBefore":4.9,"hoursAfter":3.93,"hoursChange":-0.198,"leaseBefore":65.83,"leaseAfter":54.12,"relBefore":-23767512,"relAfter":3581828,"relPaid2019":0.107,"relPaid2025":0.059,"citesBefore":1,"citesAfter":0,"peersHoursChange":0.028},{"home":"Atherton Park Post-Acute","city":"Menlo Park","changed":"2019-08-01","buyer":"Carpinteria LLC","seller":"Calcare Inc","before":2018,"after":2025,"hoursBefore":4.09,"hoursAfter":3.64,"hoursChange":-0.11,"leaseBefore":31.88,"leaseAfter":59.68,"relBefore":636164,"relAfter":9478086,"relPaid2019":0.054,"relPaid2025":0.064,"citesBefore":0,"citesAfter":0,"peersHoursChange":0.068},{"home":"Santa Clara Post Acute","city":"Santa Clara","changed":"2022-05-01","buyer":"991 Clyde Avenue Opco, LLC","seller":"Tlc Of The Bay Area Inc","before":2021,"after":2025,"hoursBefore":4.31,"hoursAfter":3.78,"hoursChange":-0.124,"leaseBefore":30.88,"leaseAfter":25.11,"relBefore":0,"relAfter":4128598,"relPaid2019":0.016,"relPaid2025":0.063,"citesBefore":2,"citesAfter":6,"peersHoursChange":0.027},{"home":"Golden Pavilion Healthcare","city":"Daly City","changed":"2021-04-08","buyer":"Golden Pavilion Operations, LLC","seller":"Ghc Of Daly City 239, LLC","before":2020,"after":2025,"hoursBefo